{
 "contract": "#156/#225 common rendering contract (Home, App Core, OS Product), one class per scenario: cards (a complete same-user list, shown whole), empty (complete and empty: genuine 'No background work'), loading (not reported yet), cannot_confirm (any part of Rose's scope incomplete, in flight or more than one Rose session: no app cards), unreadable (malformed or failed read: no app cards), locked (no app cards). No class except cards shows an app card.",
 "controller": "dev.pixel.backgroundcontrol",
 "controllerUid": 10123,
 "user": 0,
 "note": "Consumer half: snapshots are what the producer sends (complete, per registration, generation rising on every change); sessionDevices is getVirtualDevices() COMPUTER_CONTROL display->device as read; released are session displays seen before and gone now. expect is the Launcher3 row. Synthetic ids and packages, not captured output. Each device snapshot is followed by the same dispatch's onAutomatedDeviceAppsChanged at the same generation: its apps are given explicitly, or (when the producer is current) are the scenario's tasks of the owner's user on that device; appsMissing means the second callback has not arrived yet.",
